### Tier 2: Essential Defenses (15 minutes)
**If you MUST use Java serialization for legacy reasons**

**Option A: Use ObjectInputFilter (Java 9+)**

Java 9+ includes ObjectInputFilter to restrict what classes can be deserialized:

```java
import java.io.ObjectInputFilter;
import java.io.ObjectInputStream;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.Set;

@Service
public class SafeLegacySerializationService {

    private static final Set<String> ALLOWED_CLASSES = new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList(
        "com.myapp.User",
        "com.myapp.UserRole",
        "java.util.ArrayList",
        "java.util.HashMap",
        "java.lang.String",
        "java.lang.Long",
        "java.lang.Integer"
        // WHITELIST ONLY safe classes - deny everything else
    ));

    public Object deserializeFromRedis(byte[] data) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        ByteArrayInputStream bais = new ByteArrayInputStream(data);
        ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(bais);

        // SECURE: Reject any class not in allowlist
        ObjectInputFilter filter = ObjectInputFilter.Config.createFilter(
            "com.myapp.* & !com.myapp.DangerousClass;" +
            "java.util.* & !java.lang.ProcessBuilder;" +
            "java.lang.String;" +
            "java.lang.Long;" +
            "java.lang.Integer;" +
            "maxarray=10000;"  // Prevent billion-byte attack
        );

        ois.setObjectInputFilter(filter);

        try {
            return ois.readObject();
        } finally {
            ois.close();
        }
    }
}
```

**Option B: Use Apache Commons IO with DisabledObjectInputStream**

```java
import org.apache.commons.io.serialization.ValidatingObjectInputStream;

public Object deserializeFromRedis(byte[] data) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
    ByteArrayInputStream bais = new ByteArrayInputStream(data);
    ValidatingObjectInputStream ois = new ValidatingObjectInputStream(bais);

    // SECURE: Only allow specific safe classes
    ois.accept(
        "com.myapp.User",
        "com.myapp.UserRole",
        "java.util.ArrayList",
        "java.util.HashMap",
        "java.lang.String"
    );

    try {
        return ois.readObject();
    } finally {
        ois.close();
    }
}
```

**Option C: Use Kryo Serialization (Safer than Java native)**

Kryo is a fast serialization framework with better control:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.esotericsoftware</groupId>
    <artifactId>kryo</artifactId>
    <version>5.4.0</version>
</dependency>
```

```java
import com.esotericsoftware.kryo.Kryo;
import com.esotericsoftware.kryo.io.Input;
import com.esotericsoftware.kryo.io.Output;

@Service
public class KryoSerializationService {

    private final Kryo kryo = new Kryo();

    public KryoSerializationService() {
        // SECURE: Whitelist only safe classes
        kryo.setRegistrationRequired(true);  // Require explicit registration
        kryo.register(User.class);
        kryo.register(UserRole.class);
        kryo.register(ArrayList.class);
        kryo.register(HashMap.class);
    }

    public void serializeUser(User user, ByteArrayOutputStream out) {
        Output output = new Output(out);
        kryo.writeObject(output, user);
        output.close();
    }

    public User deserializeUser(byte[] data) {
        Input input = new Input(new ByteArrayInputStream(data));
        User user = kryo.readObject(input, User.class);
        input.close();
        return user;
    }
}
```

